{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/infantilisation",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "infantilisation"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "Treatment that reduces an adult person to the status of a minor, denying her authority, privacy, sexuality and decision-making capacity."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "In the context of disability, it can include using a childish tone, making decisions for someone without consulting them, or assuming they cannot understand or express their own preferences. It characteristically affects persons with disabilities – and, in an aggravated way, women with disabilities –who are portrayed as eternal minors, asexual or incapable of forming a judgement, which may serve to justify paternalism, the substitution of their will and the restriction of their sexual, reproductive and participation rights. It is not benevolent care, but a form of discrimination based on stereotypes that heightens exposure to violence and abuse. International law requires combating it: the CRPD requires action against stereotypes and prejudices (art. 8), recognises legal capacity on an equal basis (art. 12) and places the person's autonomy and dignity at its core (art. 3)."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "1.8"
  ],
